/*****************************************************************************
    displayFormT -- THE INTERPRETER POP FOR displayForm.  Step 0, Tony + Clay
    addendum 2026-08-04.

    PURPOSE, and the scope is deliberately narrow: pin what displayForm PRINTS,
    under the interpreter, against a tree that exercises more than the happy
    path. Tony's own tests in IncantForms/WorkingOn/tester pass and are
    happy-path by design; this is the exhaustiveness half.

    ⚠ STANDING RULE, TONY'S: NO ERROR-HUNTING ON WORKING CODE. Whatever this
    prints, once correctly reviewed, IS the baseline. Nothing here is hardened
    speculatively, nothing is "fixed" on the way past, and no assertion claims
    the output is right in any sense beyond "this is what it does today".

    ⚠ THE ACTION IS COPIED VERBATIM from IncantForms/WorkingOn/tester. It is not
    tidied, not reformatted and not improved -- a baseline captured over an
    edited copy would pin the edit, not the code. If displayForm changes there,
    this copy is stale and the diff is the notification.

    THE TREE COVERS THE THREE CASES THE ADDENDUM NAMES:
      1. NESTING              dfRoot -> dfMid -> dfLeaf, members within members,
                              so the recursion and the indent push/pop are both
                              exercised at depth 2.
      2. A noPrint ATTRIBUTE  dfCoded carries code={}, and aCTionDefinE attaches
                              CodE / this / tempField as noPrint attributes. That
                              is the honest way to get one -- they arise from the
                              language rather than from a flag set to make a test
                              pass -- and it puts displayForm's `if noPrinT;
                              continue;` under real load.
      3. A LEAF WITH ATTRIBUTES AND NO MEMBERS
                              dfLeaf has two attributes and nothing indented
                              under it, so the members iterate runs over an
                              empty list immediately after the attributes
                              iterate has run over a full one.

    WHAT THIS DOES NOT CERTIFY, named so the rung is not over-read:
      - unqualified iterate            -- that is incant/juiProbe's job
      - KANT-8 / recursion locals      -- needs a return-a-local fixture;
                                          displayForm prints and discards
      - anything about the JIT         -- this is pure interpreter

    ONE stop(), AT THE END, reachable only through the last section (rule H2).
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);

search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;

register(FormT);
define
    /*  THE TREE. Attributes are the bare names on the definition line; members
        are the indented definitions beneath it.  */
    dfLeaf      leafOne leafTwo;
    dfCoded     codedAttr code={ counter = counter + 1; };
    dfRoot      alpha beta gamma
        dfMid   delta epsilon
            dfInner zeta;
        dfCoded2 codedTwo code={ counter = counter + 2; };
        dfBare;
    /*  displayForm, COPIED VERBATIM from IncantForms/WorkingOn/tester.  */
    displayForm code={
        length  = listLengtH;
        print ~taG:;
        if length > 0;
            iterate grup attributes on *argument;
            while ++grup;
                if noPrinT; continue;
                if isMethoD;    print ~`taG "has method":;
                else            print ~`taG "does not have method":;
            iterate grup members on *argument;
            while ++grup;
                print +;
                displayForm(*grup);
                print $-;
        };
    ;

print "== CASE 1: a leaf -- attributes, no members ==":;
displayForm(dfLeaf);

print "== CASE 2: a coded node -- noPrint attributes must be skipped ==":;
displayForm(dfCoded);

print "== CASE 3: nesting, depth 2, with a coded member and a bare member ==":;
displayForm(dfRoot);

print "displayFormT SENTINEL -- run reached the end":;
stop();
